    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes; the Eagles lost, but their percentage increased from $68\\%$ to approximately $72.9\\%$.",
      "worked": "The Eagles lost to the Hawks, $28$ goals to $30$.\n\nBefore the game:\n$$\\begin{align*}P_{\\text{before}}&=\\frac{85}{125}\\times100\\%\\\\P_{\\text{before}}&=68\\%\\end{align*}$$\nAfter the game:\n$$\\begin{align*}P_{\\text{after}}&=\\frac{85+28}{125+30}\\times100\\%\\\\P_{\\text{after}}&=\\frac{113}{155}\\times100\\%\\\\P_{\\text{after}}&\\approx72.9\\%\\end{align*}$$\nTheir percentage increased despite the loss.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
